            <h2>Route Overview: San Diego to Los Angeles</h2>
            <p>
                Traveling from San Diego to Los Angeles by train is a convenient and scenic way to connect Southern California's two largest urban hubs. This route provides passengers with a relaxed alternative to driving or flying - especially popular for leisure travelers, students, surfers, and weekend trips. While not as fast as high-speed rail in Europe, the service offers comfortable seating, onboard amenities, and spectacular coastal views along the Pacific Ocean.
                The route is primarily served by Amtrak's Pacific Surfliner, offering multiple daily departures between San Diego's Santa Fe Depot and Los Angeles Union Station. Compared to road travel on the often-congested I-5 freeway, taking the train helps you avoid highway traffic. It makes city-to-city travel easy without worrying about parking or rental cars. The Pacific Surfliner is also famous for being one of the most scenic train routes in the United States, with large portions of the track running parallel to
                ,the coastline.
            </p>
