            <h3>What This Means for Travelers</h3>
            <p>Taking the train between San Diego and Los Angeles gives you a moderately long, laid-back travel experience. It's slower than flying but allows you to relax, use Wi-Fi, stretch your legs, and enjoy breathtaking views of the Southern California coastline - including the Pacific Ocean, coastal bluffs, and beach communities. Compared to road travel, the train avoids freeway traffic stress (especially on the heavily congested I-5 corridor through Orange County). It delivers you straight into downtown Los Angeles without needing a car. </p>

