            <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
            <h3>1. How long is the train from San Diego to Los Angeles? </h3>

            <p> The train journey typically takes 2 hours 47 minutes to 3 hours 30 minutes, depending on the service (Pacific Surfliner) and the number of stops. </p>

            <h3>2. What is the fastest train from San Diego to Los Angeles? </h3>

            <p> The fastest option is Amtrak Pacific Surfliner, which can complete the journey in approximately 2 hours 42 minutes to 2 hours 47 minutes with direct service. </p>

            <h3>3. How much does a train ticket from San Diego to Los Angeles cost? </h3>

            <p>
                Ticket prices generally fall between:
                $35-$45 for early booking
                $45-$60 for standard fares
                $60-$70+ for last-minute or Business Class travel
            </p>

            <h3>4. Are there direct trains from San Diego to Los Angeles? </h3>

            <p>Yes, all Amtrak Pacific Surfliner trains are direct, so there's no need for transfers. </p>

            <h3>5. What amenities are available onboard? </h3>

            <p>Trains offer comfortable seating, Wi-Fi (where available), power outlets, a café/bistro car with local craft beverages, and luggage space. Surfboards, bikes, and golf clubs are also permitted onboard. </p>

            <h3>6. Is train travel faster than driving? </h3>

            <p>Depending on traffic, driving may take 2-3.5 hours on I-5, while the train is generally stress-free, predictable, and scenic - especially during rush hour or beach weekends. </p>

            <h3>7. Can you travel from San Diego to Los Angeles in one day? </h3>

            <p>Yes, the route is well-suited for same-day trips, with 13+ daily departures. Early morning trains get you to Los Angeles by mid-morning, and evening trains return you to San Diego by late night. </p>

            <h3>8. Which station in San Diego do trains depart from? </h3>

            <p>Most trains depart from the San Diego Santa Fe Depot, located in downtown San Diego. Additional stops include Old Town San Diego and Sorrento Valley. </p>

            <h3>9. Which station do trains arrive at in Los Angeles? </h3>

            <p>Trains arrive at Los Angeles Union Station, conveniently located in the city center (Downtown LA) and easily accessible by Metro Rail, buses, and rideshare. </p>

            <h3>10. Is Business Class worth it? </h3>

            <p>Yes, Business Class offers extra legroom, a quieter environment, priority boarding, complimentary snacks and beverages, and a dedicated attendant - making it ideal for travelers seeking more comfort during the 2.5-3.5 hour journey. </p>







